WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.520
I want to take up in volume 6 again, and I want to begin at January 6, 1904.

2
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.560
The human race is all one family.

3
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.440
When someone does some good work and offers it to God, the whole human family

4
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:36.080
participates in that offering, and is present to God as if all were offering it.

5
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:44.000
So here we're looking now at this message in which the Lord is identifying us as part of a body.

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.840
We're part of the human race as a body and we're part of the mystical body of Christ.

7
00:00:51.840 --> 00:01:00.400
Continuing in my usual state, blessed baby Jesus came, and after He placed Himself in my arms,

8
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:10.240
and He blessed me with His little hands, He told me, "My daughter, since the human race is all one family,

9
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:19.280
when someone does some good work and offers something to me, the whole human family participates in that offering.

10
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.600
And is present to me as if all were offering it."

11
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:31.680
So this is the preparation for teaching us how to operate in the divine will.

12
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:41.280
As for example, today, as the maid I offered their gifts to me, I had all human generations present in their persons,

13
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.240
and all participated in the merit of their good work.

14
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:57.840
The first thing they offered to me was gold, and I in return gave them the intelligence and the knowledge of truth, which is His gold.

15
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:06.400
But do you know which gold I want from souls? It's not material gold. It's spiritual gold. It is the gold of their will,

16
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:16.080
the gold of their affections of their desires of their own tastes, and the gold of the whole interior of man.

17
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:22.320
This is all the gold that the soul has, and I want all of it for myself.

18
00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:35.600
That's the exclusive love that God has the right to demand of us, and you find the text in Deuteronomy 6, 4 to 10.

19
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:46.400
Also in John 7 verses 38 and 39, Jesus says that if you are thirsty and you really want communion with God, then come to Him.

20
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:54.240
Now, it's almost difficult for the soul to give this to me without sacrificing and mortifying herself.

21
00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:01.920
So we have to give ourselves, we can't hold on to ourselves and say we're in union with God.

22
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:12.720
And this is how mirror-like electric wire binds the interior of man and renders it more shining and gives it the shades of multiple colors,

23
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:25.120
giving all species of beauty to the soul. But this is not all. It takes someone who maintains the colors and the freshness always alive,

24
00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:35.520
which almost like fragrance and breeze blow from within the soul. It takes someone who offers and obtains greater gifts than the ones that he gives.

25
00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:46.240
It also takes someone who forces the one who receives and the one who gives to dwell in his own interior, keeping him a continuous conversation

26
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:57.440
and in continuous commerce with himself. So that's Matthew 11, 12. The kingdom of God suffers violence and the valiant take it by force.

27
00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:05.760
So who does all this? It is prayer, especially the spirit of interior prayer. That means contemplation.

28
00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:13.280
And contemplation means being completely silent in the depth of your being to commune with the silence of God,

29
00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:24.480
where the communication is just simply total. It is prayer, especially the spirit of interior prayer, which knows how to convert into gold,

30
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:32.880
not only the internal works, but also the external works. And so this is the incense.

31
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:42.800
So I want to give you Revelation 8, verses 3 to 5, that our prayer goes up like incense in the presence of God.

32
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:50.160
So we now move on to February 7, 1904, and I have a VIP on this one.

33
00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:59.520
How difficult it is to find a soul who gives all of herself to God, so that God may give all of himself to her.

34
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:08.160
This is the challenge all the time. God is looking for us to give the whole of ourselves, so that he can give the whole of himself.

35
00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.680
So that's the challenge of Deuteronomy 6, 4 to 10.

36
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:26.000
"Hero Israel, the Lord your God is one Lord, and you shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, and all your soul, all your mind, and all your being."

37
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:32.320
So Louisa said, "I spent the whole of last month in much suffering. Therefore I am Is it writing?

38
00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:42.640
And as I continue to feel very much in suffering, very often a fear comes to me that it isn't that I cannot write, but that I do not want to."

39
00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:50.400
And as an excuse, I say that I cannot. This is a very important thing. Louisa here is making a very important confession.

40
00:05:50.400 --> 00:06:02.240
We know from Volume 1 that she did not want to write. We know also from all the volumes that continue from there that she certainly didn't want any of this to go public.

41
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:15.240
So it's her own reluctance to write, and so if she's suffering, then the suffering gives her a good excuse not to do it anyway, so she's being very honest here.

42
00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:24.880
Indeed, it's true that I feel great repugnance, and I must make a great effort to write, and only obedience could conquer me.

43
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:37.760
So in order to remove any doubt, I decided to write not everything, but only a few words that I remember to see whether I cannot do it or not.

44
00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:46.000
Now, Jesus is going to keep after her, and so will the priests keep after her to write everything, not to leave anything out.

45
00:06:46.000 --> 00:07:01.280
She herself has no idea what God's plans are for her. So what she writes about in the next paragraph is the necessity of victim's souls for the church and the world.

46
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:10.480
I remember that one day, as I was feeling ill, he told me, "My daughter, what will happen if the music ceases in the world?"

47
00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:18.320
Louisa said, "Lord, what music should cease?" She doesn't seem to realize he's speaking symbolically.

48
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:29.040
And he added, "My beloved, your music," in other words, if the work that Louisa is doing stops what on earth would happen to the world,

49
00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:37.120
because he tells her in the higher volumes that the whole of Europe is depending on her.

50
00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:51.520
In fact, when the soul suffers from me, when she prays, repairs, praises, thanks continually, this is continuous music in my hearing,

51
00:07:51.520 --> 00:08:01.280
which takes me away from hearing the iniquity of the earth, and therefore from chastising as appropriate, not only this,

52
00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:08.160
but it is music in the human minds, and it diverts them from doing worse things.

53
00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:15.680
So, if I take you in death understood, would the music not cease?

54
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:21.280
For me, it's nothing, because it would be nothing other than transporting it from earth to heaven,

55
00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:27.760
and instead of having it on the earth, I'd have it in heaven, but how would the world be able to go on?

56
00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:39.920
Now, what he's trying to get through to her is that it is utterly, completely essential for the survival of the human race that there are victims' souls.

57
00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:48.960
Louisa said, "But I was thinking to myself, 'These are the usual pretexts of not to take me in death understood.'"

58
00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:56.800
There are so many good souls in the world, who do so much for God, and among all of them,

59
00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:04.480
I perhaps occupy the last place, and yet he says that if he takes me, the music would cease.

60
00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:12.160
There are so many who do it better for him. She's speaking out of humility here.

61
00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:18.080
And while I was thinking of this, he came like a flash in the ad at my daughter, what you say is true.

62
00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:25.120
But there are many good souls who do much for me, but how difficult it is to find one who gives me everything.

63
00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:33.200
That's the problem. You can have people who are good, but they're good to themselves as well as good to everybody else.

64
00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:46.240
And you have heroic people like Padre Pio, who explained that God was able to work many miracles through him, because he said, "I refuse him nothing, and he refuses me nothing."

65
00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:59.040
What God can do through one person who gives themselves fully, completely, totally to him, is absolutely out of our minds what we could even imagine.

66
00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:08.320
So if a soul gives everything to me so that I may give all of myself, that's your Deuteronomy 6, 4 to 10.

67
00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:14.400
Some retain a little bit of love of self. You see, this is why the rest of us aren't saints.

68
00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:23.840
Some keep a little bit of self-esteem. Some want affection, even be it for holy people. Some keep a little vanity.

69
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:31.680
Some retain a little bit of attachment to the earth, and some keep some interest.

70
00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:38.400
In other words, some a little thing, some another, all keeping something of their own.

71
00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:48.800
And this impedes that everything be divine in them. In other words, this blocks everything becoming divine in them.

72
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:54.160
So it's up to ourselves whether we truly enter into the divine will or not.

73
00:10:54.160 --> 00:11:02.880
We can decide whether we want to be people who experience God fully or simply experience God partially.

74
00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:11.600
The decision is ours, we have free will. St. John of the Cross says that if a bird is tied to a tree, it's a captive.

75
00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:16.160
But does it matter whether it's tied with a rope or a thread?

76
00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:23.760
In fact, it does matter because it's a much greater tragedy to be tied with a thread.

77
00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:32.320
And that's the problem of good people. That it's something small. That's what he says, a little vanity, a little affection, a little this, a little that.

78
00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:41.680
And so it's much more tragic. So Jesus continues, "Since what comes from them is not fully divine,

79
00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:47.920
their music will not be able to produce those effects to my hearing and to the human minds.

80
00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:53.360
So since it's not a completely pure gift, it cannot have the same effect.

81
00:11:53.360 --> 00:12:07.360
Therefore, their much doing will not be able to produce those effects nor please me as much as the little doing of one who keeps nothing for herself and who gives herself completely to me."

82
00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:17.840
Now, that's a message that is extremely important and decides whether we're going forward or backwards.

83
00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:24.240
Now, February the 8th, 1904, I have a VIP on this as well.

84
00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:28.480
One of the qualities of Jesus is pain.

85
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:37.640
For one who lives of his most holy will, purgatory does not exist. This is a very, very important revelation.

86
00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:50.640
Louisa said, "I remember that the other day as I continue to feel in suffering, I saw the confessor praying to our Lord to touch the part where I was suffering so as to have the sufferings mitigated.

87
00:12:50.640 --> 00:13:04.320
And blessed Jesus told me, "My daughter, your confessor wants me to touch you to alleviate your pains, but among my many qualities, I am also pain.

88
00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:18.920
And if I touch you, instead of decreasing, your pain would increase because Louisa has been called to be an earthly reflection of Jesus and to imitate him as much as possible in his life."

89
00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:37.560
In fact, Jesus said, "The thing in which my humanity delighted most was suffering, and it still delights in communicating it to those whom it loves."

90
00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:48.880
Now, we don't enjoy suffering, and when Jesus said he delighted in suffering, he's not saying he didn't feel the pain and that his human nature didn't feel the way we feel about pain.

91
00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:59.880
You have to go to Hebrews, chapter 12, verse 2, and there you read that, "For the joy that was set before him, he endured the cross, despising the shame."

92
00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:10.880
Now, you know if you do the hours of the passion that Jesus went through the most horrendous sufferings, and he felt every single last bit of it.

93
00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:18.680
When he says here that he delighted in suffering, what he means is that he could purchase the redemption of the human race through suffering.

94
00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:34.680
He could really do something powerful with it, and the victim's souls are the ones who understand more than the rest of us just how powerful suffering is for redeeming souls.

95
00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:50.680
And so he continues, "And it seemed that in reality, Louisa says, that he would touch me and make me feel more pain. So I added my sweet good, as for myself I want nothing but your most holy will.

96
00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.680
That's the way we have to be in divine will.

97
00:14:54.680 --> 00:15:03.680
I do not look at whether I suffer or I enjoy. Your will is everything for me, and it has to be everything for us as well."

98
00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:22.680
And he added, "And this is what I want. Jesus added, this is what I want. This is my design upon you, and this is enough for me and content me that we would absolutely want his holy will in everything.

99
00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:31.680
This is the greatest and the most honorable worship that a creature can render me, and that she owes me as her creator.

100
00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:39.680
And as the soul does, so it can be said that her mind lives and thinks in my mind."

101
00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:48.680
Now, you see, St. Paul tells us that we have to have the mind of Christ. It's absolutely essential.

102
00:15:48.680 --> 00:16:01.680
Being in mind, look through my eyes, her mouth speaks through my mouth, her heart loves through mine, her hands operate within my own hands, her feet within my own feet.

103
00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:15.680
So this is 1 Corinthians 12, verses 1 to 12, that we are each one of us, a cell in the body of Christ, and everything we do should be through him with him and in him,

104
00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:20.680
and he should be the origin of everything we do, okay?

105
00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:25.680
Also, I want to give you 1 Corinthians, chapter 1, verse 30 as well.

106
00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:37.680
Now, you can see that if we're operating through him with him and in him, in the divine will, he's operating through us with us and in us,

107
00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:50.680
because we've already read that we've become a little incarnation in inverted commas, that he actually bi-locates his life in us.

108
00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:57.680
And Jesus continues, he says, "And I can say, 'You are my eye, my mouth, my heart, my hands, and my feet.'"

109
00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:09.680
So again, you have your John 14, verses 20 to 21, "You and me and I in you."

110
00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:19.680
And likewise, the soul can say, "Jesus Christ is my eye, my mouth, my heart, my hands, and my feet."

111
00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:27.680
Being in this union, not only of wills, but this personal union.

112
00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:35.680
Being in this union, not only of wills, but a personal, when the soul dies, there is nothing left for her to be purged.

113
00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:42.680
In other words, if you reach this level of union with God, there's no purgatory left for you.

114
00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:51.680
Therefore, purgatory cannot touch her, because purgatory touches those who live outside of me, whether completely or in part.

115
00:17:51.680 --> 00:18:02.680
And so, whatever part of us, and for whatever length of time, we live outside of his divine will, all of that has to be purged, it has to be cleansed at some point.

116
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:12.680
It's much better to have a cleansed in this life, rather than in purgatory, because in purgatory it is extremely intense.

117
00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:24.680
So, February 12, 1904, when the soul is identified with the humanity of Jesus, none of her works are dispersed.

118
00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.680
Okay, the very important text.

119
00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:34.680
"Continue in my usual state," Louisa said, "with more suffering, blessed Jesus came.

120
00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:44.680
And from all parts of his humanity, many rivulets of light came out, which communicated themselves to all the parts of my body.

121
00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:54.680
And from these rivulets that I received, as many other rivulets came out of myself, which communicated themselves to the humanity of the Lord.

122
00:18:54.680 --> 00:19:03.680
In the meantime, I found myself surrounded by a multitude of saints who, looking at me, were saying among themselves,

123
00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:11.680
"If the Lord does not concur with the miracle, she will no longer be able to live, because she lacks the vital humours."

124
00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:25.680
Now, what the saints are saying is that Louisa is becoming so spiritualized that unless the Lord really does something, she won't be able to stay on the earth. It won't be possible.

125
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:32.680
The circulation of her blood is no longer natural, therefore, according to the natural laws, she must die.

126
00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:35.680
Now, that would make Louisa very happy.

127
00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:42.680
And they were praying, blessed Jesus, to make this miracle that I might continue to live. And the Lord said to them,

128
00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:54.680
"The communications of the rivulets, as you see, means that everything she does, even the natural things, are identified with my humanity."

129
00:19:54.680 --> 00:20:08.680
And when I make the soul reach this point of spirituality understood, of everything that both soul and body do, nothing is dispersed, everything remains in May.

130
00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:25.680
There's no wastage of time, of desires, of motivations, of actions, of words, of prayers, or anything, it's the most incredible thing.

131
00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:41.680
Many works of hers are, in fact, dispersed. But since I made Louisa reach this point, why can I not take her?

132
00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:52.680
Now, while he was saying this, I said to myself, this is Louisa speaking, it seems that everyone is against me. Obedience doesn't want me to die.

133
00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:59.680
These saints are praying that the Lord will not take me. What do they want from me?

134
00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:09.680
You see, we're still only in volume six, so Louisa hasn't yet received the full revelation of the divine will, which is in volumes 11 and 12,

135
00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:19.680
in which she will begin to comprehend in some way the enormity of the mission that Jesus is giving to her.

136
00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:27.680
I don't know why they want me to be on the earth, almost by force, far away from my highest good, and she said I was all afflicted.

137
00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:35.680
And while I was thinking of this, Jesus said, my daughter, please don't want to afflict yourself. In other words, don't put your will into it now.

138
00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:44.680
I know you're not feeling wonderful. The things of the world are most sad, and they will get worse and worse.

139
00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:50.680
Now, the worse and worse is World War I, World War II, and everything else.

140
00:21:50.680 --> 00:22:00.680
If the point comes from me to give free vent to my justice, I will take you, and then I will no longer listen to anyone.

141
00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:12.680
Now, here he's telling Louisa how important her position is as the person who stands in the breach between the justice of God and the sinfulness of the human race.

142
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:19.680
Now, poor Louisa can't see that she's all that important, and all she wants is to be with the Lord.

143
00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:26.680
But he's saying to her that we'll be tied the earth if you die. It's very serious.

144
00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:30.680
And she did die after the Second World War.

145
00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:35.680
So let's come to February the 21st, 1904.

146
00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:40.680
The promise of Louisa if she is allowed to die.

147
00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:51.680
In the presence of the Most Holy Trinity, of the Most Holy Mother Mary, of my guardian angel, and of the whole celestial court, and in order to obey my confessor,

148
00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:57.680
I promise that if the Lord in his infinite mercy should give me the grace of letting me die,

149
00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:06.680
when I find myself together with my celestial spouse, I will pray and plead for the triumph of Holy Mother Church,

150
00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:10.680
and the confusion and conversion of our enemies.

151
00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:15.680
That the Catholic party that's in Italy may triumph in our country,

152
00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:22.680
and that the Church of St. Cataldo may be reopened for service. That's in the town of Corrato.

153
00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:31.680
And that my confessor be freed of his usual sufferings with the Holy freedom of spirit and the sanctity of a true apostle of our Lord.

154
00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:41.680
And that always if the Lord permits, I will go to him at least once a month to confer about celestial things and things pertaining to the good of my soul.

155
00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:45.680
I promise all this for my part, and I swear.

156
00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:48.680
Now that's only 1904.

157
00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:51.680
And this is only Volume 6.

158
00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:59.680
There are 30 more volumes for her to accomplish, and she will have changed so radically.

159
00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:03.680
She will have a completely different approach when she's going back to God.

160
00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:12.680
She will realize she has to take the human race with her and not just have her own private little once and desires.

161
00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:21.680
Now we're all like that. We all start from a very small base, and we're concerned only with the people immediately around us.

162
00:24:21.680 --> 00:24:33.680
And it's on a slow step-by-step basis that the Lord moves us onto a higher platform until he gets us to think in terms of the whole of humanity all the time,

163
00:24:33.680 --> 00:24:38.680
so that we're praying the way he wants us to pray.

164
00:24:38.680 --> 00:24:52.680
So February the 22nd, 1904, the great gift of having a victim's soul.

165
00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.680
And I saw people who were suffering.

166
00:24:54.680 --> 00:25:00.680
I prayed Jesus to free them of those sufferings, even at the cost of suffering myself in their place.

167
00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:07.680
And he said to me, "If you want to suffer yourself now, that you are a victim, fine."

168
00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:22.680
Because then, when the victim comes to me, those who surround you, your own country and even kingdoms will see the void that they will feel.

169
00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:29.680
Oh, how they will know then through this loss, the great good that I have given to them in giving them a victim.

170
00:25:29.680 --> 00:25:41.680
So here Jesus is trying to tell Louisa how desperately important it is for her to do her victim role, victim soul role in the world.

171
00:25:41.680 --> 00:25:54.680
So February the 12th, 1904, Louisa speaks about some priests about the church of St. Cataldo, so she's still onto local stuff.

172
00:25:54.680 --> 00:26:00.680
When you get to the higher volumes, she's only talking about divine will.

173
00:26:00.680 --> 00:26:13.680
Louisa said, "I'd forgotten to say what I'm about to write, which is, I will say now, out of obedience, although these are not sure things, but uncertain because the presence of our Lord was missing.

174
00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:34.680
I was outside of myself and I seemed to find myself inside a church in which there were several venerable priests and also sold from purgatory, and holy people conversing among themselves about the church of St. Cataldo, saying that almost with certainty it would be obtained.

175
00:26:34.680 --> 00:26:42.680
On hearing this I said, "How can this be?" The other day it was rumored that the chapter had lost the cause.

176
00:26:42.680 --> 00:26:53.680
So through the tribunal it could not be obtained, the town council does not want to give it, and you are saying that it will be obtained.

177
00:26:53.680 --> 00:27:08.680
And they added, "In spite of all the difficulties, indeed it is not lost." So Louisa is being reminded that we have to each one of us learn how to trust God beyond reason.

178
00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:20.680
And even if they reach the point of laying hands on it to knock it down, it still cannot be considered as lost because St. Cataldo will know well how to defend his temple.

179
00:27:20.680 --> 00:27:34.680
However, poor Corrato, if they arrive at this. And while saying this they are repeated, they have taken away the first things the crowned lady has already been transported to his house.

180
00:27:34.680 --> 00:27:56.680
The crowned lady would be Blessed Virgin. You go before our lady and pray to her that having started the grace she would fulfill it. I went out of that church to go and pray, but as I was doing this she said, "I found myself within myself." In other words, out of the ecstasy.

181
00:27:56.680 --> 00:28:05.680
So that's about a local church in her area. So March the 4th, 1904, I have a VIP on this one as well.

182
00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:16.680
In other words, the Lord explains here that we must become eagles and we must fly high in his presence. Okay.

183
00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:23.680
So the soul must live up high. One who lives up high cannot be harmed.

184
00:28:23.680 --> 00:28:31.680
As I was very afflicted and in suffering because of the loss of my good Jesus, Louisa said, I saw him for just a little.

185
00:28:31.680 --> 00:28:47.680
And he told me, "My daughter, your soul must try to maintain the flight of the eagle. That is to dwell up high above all the low things of this earth, and so high that no enemy may harm it.

186
00:28:47.680 --> 00:28:58.680
And therefore we have to realize that people called to live in the heights of the divine will are eagles. It's something we have to look into.

187
00:28:58.680 --> 00:29:05.680
And the eagle lives so high that her young are very safe from all predators.

188
00:29:05.680 --> 00:29:20.680
In fact, one who lives up high can harm the enemies, but cannot be harmed themselves. And she must not only live up high, but she must try to have purity and sharpness of the eye.

189
00:29:20.680 --> 00:29:29.680
The eagle is famous for that sharpness of the eye, the incredible vision that they have from a great height that they can actually see fish in the ocean.

190
00:29:29.680 --> 00:29:55.680
So similar to those of the eagle. So I want to give you a number of scriptures for this. Deuteronomy 32 verses 10 to 12, Proverbs 30 verse 19, Jeremiah 48, 40, and Ephesians 6 from verse 10 to 20.

191
00:29:55.680 --> 00:30:09.680
Through living up high, Jesus said, through the sharpness of her sight, she penetrates into divine things. That's your Matthew 5, 8, the pure in heart, see God.

192
00:30:09.680 --> 00:30:20.680
So she penetrates into divine things not in passing, but by chewing them to the point of making of them her favorite food, despising any other thing.

193
00:30:20.680 --> 00:30:28.680
And she also penetrates the necessities of her neighbor, nor is she afraid to descend into their midst and to do good to them.

194
00:30:28.680 --> 00:30:44.680
And if indeed she lays down her life, and if needed she lays down her life. Through the purity of her sight, she makes the love of God and the love of neighbor from two into one law, rectifying everything in God.

195
00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:55.680
So must the soul be if she wants to please me. What Jesus has just said there is that we must live Matthew 22 verses 22 to 24.

196
00:30:55.680 --> 00:31:04.680
That loving God and neighbor are two sides of one reality, and you cannot have one without the other.

197
00:31:04.680 --> 00:31:18.680
And if we think we can live a divine life in the divine will without loving others, then we are completely deceived. It's not going to work.

198
00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:38.680
So March the 5th, 1904, the Lord gives us a wake up call. He calls it a citation, obviously that was legal language in his own day. The cross he says is a citation, an advocate and a judge for the soul, so that she may take possession of the eternal kingdom.

199
00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:55.680
So somebody might be going along having a wonderful time really enjoying life, and they're not thinking of eternal realities at all. And so the Lord has to give them a wake up call so that they begin to think properly and begin to move in the direction the Lord wants.

200
00:31:55.680 --> 00:32:16.680
So Louisa says this morning I was feeling in much suffering with the addition of Jesus' privation. Then after I struggled very much, he came for just a few instances and he told me, my daughter, sufferings, crosses are like many citations which I send to souls.

201
00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:37.680
A citation is a summons or a call, just like you get a summons from the police. If the soul accepts these wake up calls, I call them, whether they are citations that notify the soul to pay some debt, in other words to make reparation for something that you need to repair,

202
00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:57.680
or is a notification to obtain some gain for eternal life, that he wants you to do something to enhance your spiritual life. If the soul responds to me by resigning herself to my will, by thanking me, by adoring my holy dispositions,

203
00:32:57.680 --> 00:33:09.680
we are immediately in accord, and the soul will avoid many inconveniences that are possible like being cited again.

204
00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:25.680
Having advocates involved, going through the suit and receiving the condemnation of the judge, in other words, you put aside all judgment by actually accepting the summons that's given to you and responding to it

205
00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:34.680
and reminding yourself that the Lord shouldn't have to send you a summons the next time.

206
00:33:34.680 --> 00:33:48.680
So to avoid the judgment, then she has to respond to the Lord. So responding to the citation with resignation and with thanksgiving alone will make up for all of this,

207
00:33:48.680 --> 00:33:59.680
because the cross will be the citation, advocate and judge for that soul, with nothing else needed for her to take possession of the eternal kingdom.

208
00:33:59.680 --> 00:34:07.680
So by just accepting and surrendering to the cross that the Lord has given to us, that in itself does all the work.

209
00:34:07.680 --> 00:34:25.680
If then she refuses these citations, think about it yourself into how many abysses of disgrace and trouble she can throw herself into and what the rigor of the judge will be in condemning her for having shunned the cross as her judge.

210
00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:37.680
That's Matthew 1624, when Peter rejected the cross and Jesus very severely pushed him aside and told him that the cross was for everyone.

211
00:34:37.680 --> 00:34:48.680
The cross is so much milder, more compassionate, more prone to enriching her rather than judging her, more intent on embellishing rather than condemning her.

212
00:34:48.680 --> 00:35:01.680
So what we're being told here is that while the cross is difficult for us, at the same time the Lord is saying that it's incredible mercy,

213
00:35:01.680 --> 00:35:11.680
that he's still interested in working with us and he still thinks you have a future spiritually and he still thinks that you would be willing to grow.

214
00:35:11.680 --> 00:35:24.680
So, March the 12th, 1904, here we hear of threats of wars, all Europe lies on Louise's shoulders, that's what I said to you earlier.

215
00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:37.680
Even before we start I want to give you Amos, AMOS37, and it says that the Lord never does anything without telling the prophets first.

216
00:35:37.680 --> 00:35:43.680
When people become very close to the Lord, he tells them his secrets.

217
00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:54.680
Since Louise is ill, I imposed on her to dictate to me, so this is the priest actually writing this, very unusual.

218
00:35:54.680 --> 00:35:59.680
As she could not disobey, she dictated what follows with great repugnance.

219
00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:07.680
As I lamented to our Lord that while I felt in suffering, he would still not take me to heaven.

220
00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:11.680
Blessed Jesus told me, my daughter have courage in suffering.

221
00:36:11.680 --> 00:36:18.680
I do not want you to afflict yourself in seeing yourself not yet taken to heaven.

222
00:36:18.680 --> 00:36:30.680
You must know that all Europe lies on your shoulders, and the good or bad outcome for Europe depends on your sufferings.

223
00:36:30.680 --> 00:36:34.680
Now the Lord kept her on the earth until after the Second World War.

224
00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:42.680
She had to hold Europe together in two world wars, that was some task.

225
00:36:42.680 --> 00:36:53.680
If you are strong and constant in suffering, things will be more bearable, the wars will still happen, but things won't be as hellish as they could have been.

226
00:36:53.680 --> 00:37:08.680
If you are not strong and constant in suffering, or if I take you to heaven, things will be so grave that Europe will be threatened with invasion and being seized by foreigners.

227
00:37:08.680 --> 00:37:25.680
Even more he added, if you remain on earth and suffer much with desire and constancy, all the chastisements that will happen in Europe will serve for the coming triumph of Holy Mother Church.

228
00:37:25.680 --> 00:37:42.680
Now notice the way he gives her the incentive to sit there day after day, day after interminable day, suffering and suffering and suffering when she cannot see what the result is going to be.

229
00:37:42.680 --> 00:37:46.680
So he tells her ahead of time.

230
00:37:46.680 --> 00:38:00.680
So it will serve for the triumph of Mother Church. And if in spite of all this, Europe will not take advantage and will remain obstinate in sin, your sufferings will serve as preparation for your own death.

231
00:38:00.680 --> 00:38:09.680
In other words, nothing will be lost in the Kingdom of God and in the Divine will, nothing is ever, ever lost.

232
00:38:09.680 --> 00:38:20.680
And so if Europe doesn't take advantage, it will all go back to yourself. And so Father Genaro De Genaro signs that.

233
00:38:20.680 --> 00:38:33.680
So March the 14th, 1904. Because of the necessity of the times, Jesus asks for silence as he wants to chastise.

234
00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:43.680
As I was in my usual state, after I struggled very much, blessed Jesus came out from within my interior because he's there all the time.

235
00:38:43.680 --> 00:38:50.680
And as I wanted to speak, he placed a finger on my mouth telling me be quiet, be quiet.

236
00:38:50.680 --> 00:38:54.680
It's hard for an Italian to actually keep silence.

237
00:38:54.680 --> 00:39:08.680
I was left so very mortified, she said, and no longer dared to open my mouth. And blessed Jesus, seeing me so mortified, added dearest daughter of mine, the necessity of the times demands silence.

238
00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:17.680
Because if you speak to me, your word binds my hands, and I never come to deeds chastising as appropriate.

239
00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:27.680
And so we're always at the beginning. In other words, the human race has not been chastised sufficiently for it to grow.

240
00:39:27.680 --> 00:39:39.680
And if it doesn't grow, it will disintegrate. Therefore Jesus said, "It's necessary that there be silence between you and me for some time."

241
00:39:39.680 --> 00:39:53.680
And while he was saying this, a sign came out with words written on it and it said, "It is decreed, scourges, pains and wars," and he disappeared.

242
00:39:53.680 --> 00:40:18.680
So here is Louisa being told that she doesn't have a choice. She must actually cooperate with him if she's choosing his divine will. And he sees that it is the most important thing to chastise the human race because there's no other thing that can happen if they're to turn back to him and begin living correctly.

243
00:40:18.680 --> 00:40:23.680
Then she must agree with that. She finds that very difficult.

244
00:40:23.680 --> 00:40:34.680
So March the 16th, 1904, true resignation does not put things under scrutiny. In other words, you don't rationalise them. You just surrender.

245
00:40:34.680 --> 00:40:44.680
But adores in silence the divine dispositions. The cross is festive, jubilant, joyful and desiring.

246
00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:57.680
Now most of us don't look at the cross that way. So Louisa says this morning, as I was in my usual state, I found myself over a person who appeared as though clothed like a sheep.

247
00:40:57.680 --> 00:41:11.680
And I was carried on his shoulders. But he walked at a slow pace while in front of him there was something like a car. Very interesting cars were just invented at the time.

248
00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:16.680
Which was faster. And I said in my interior, this one is going slowly.

249
00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:26.680
I would like to go inside the car and go faster. That's the way all of us feel about things we would prefer to get wherever we're going as fast as we can.

250
00:41:26.680 --> 00:41:32.680
In other words, the way the world does things seems better. Oh dear.

251
00:41:32.680 --> 00:41:43.680
I don't know why, but as soon as I thought of this, I found myself there inside of this car with other people who said to me, what have you done? You've left the shepherd.

252
00:41:43.680 --> 00:41:56.680
And what a shepherd. In fact, since his life is in the fields, all the medicinal herbs, noxious and solitary are his.

253
00:41:56.680 --> 00:42:02.680
And by being with him, one can be always in good health.

254
00:42:02.680 --> 00:42:12.680
And if you see him clothed like a sheep, it is so that he can make himself similar to the sheep. Colossians 1.20.

255
00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:18.680
Allowing them to approach him with no fear. And even though he walks at a slow pace, it's safer.

256
00:42:18.680 --> 00:42:28.680
So this message is obviously not given for Louisa personally. It's for us. All the poor folk that are hoping to follow in our footsteps.

257
00:42:28.680 --> 00:42:35.680
Because the inclination to turn back to the world and to do things the world's way is with us all the time.

258
00:42:35.680 --> 00:42:47.680
It wasn't necessarily with Louisa. And we know from higher volumes that a lot of the messages that she got were actually for the people coming after her.

259
00:42:47.680 --> 00:43:00.680
So Louisa said on hearing this, I said in my interior, since this is so, I would like to be with him so as to tell him something about my illness.

260
00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:09.680
But as I was thinking of this, I found him near me. And I, all content, drew close to his ear and said to him, good shepherd.

261
00:43:09.680 --> 00:43:17.680
If you are so very expert, give me some remedy for my troubles as I find myself in this state of sufferings.

262
00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:29.680
And as I wanted to say more, he cut my words inside my mouth. Why? Because the last message he asked, he said that the times were so bad that they needed to be silent.

263
00:43:29.680 --> 00:43:43.680
And typical of human beings, we think it's only for that five minutes. Or for that half hour, we don't seem to realize that the thing about silence may be going on for months.

264
00:43:43.680 --> 00:43:55.680
So he cut the words short and he said, true resignation, Jesus said. Not an imaginary one, but real resignation does not put things under scrutiny.

265
00:43:55.680 --> 00:44:09.680
But it doors in silence, the divine dispositions. Now, notice that this is at least three times that I've read those words in the last few minutes, adore the divine dispositions.

266
00:44:09.680 --> 00:44:16.680
In other words, let God be God and just simply surrender. He knows he's in charge. He knows what he's doing.

267
00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:30.680
So I wanted to put Luke 9, 23 there. And as he was saying this, it seemed that the sheep's skin split and I could see the face of our Lord and his head was actually crowned with thorns.

268
00:44:30.680 --> 00:44:37.680
On hearing him tell me that I did not know what else to say. She's supposed to keep silence.

269
00:44:37.680 --> 00:44:42.680
And so I remained in silent content to be with them. That's what he's asked her to do.

270
00:44:42.680 --> 00:44:53.680
Most of us find it difficult to just sit with the Lord and be silent with him. We prefer telling God what to do.

271
00:44:53.680 --> 00:45:01.680
And so Jesus said to her, you have forgotten to tell the confessor another thing about the cross.

272
00:45:01.680 --> 00:45:16.680
And Louisa said, my adorable Lord, I don't remember, repeated to me and I will tell him. And he said, my daughter, among the many titles that the cross has, it has the title of feast day.

273
00:45:16.680 --> 00:45:25.680
Now, none of us would ever in our wildest dreams put the word feast day on the cross.

274
00:45:25.680 --> 00:45:35.680
But I want you to put Galatians 614 beside it because St. Paul says, I glory in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ.

275
00:45:35.680 --> 00:45:44.680
And I gave you Hebrews 12 to already that for the joy that was set before him, he endured the cross despising the shame.

276
00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:51.680
One makes feast Jesus said and rejoices and is more content.

277
00:45:51.680 --> 00:45:59.680
He says, because when one receives a gift, you know, you feast and you rejoice and so on.

278
00:45:59.680 --> 00:46:16.680
Now he said, since the cross is the most precious, the noblest gift and is given by the greatest and most unique person that exists, it is more pleasing and brings more feast and more gladness than all the other gifts.

279
00:46:16.680 --> 00:46:25.680
The cross is given to us by God himself, who is pure love, 1 John 4 7.

280
00:46:25.680 --> 00:46:32.680
So our response to the cross has got to be Jesus's response to the Father in John 14 31.

281
00:46:32.680 --> 00:46:40.680
I want the world to know that I love the Father and therefore I do exactly what my Father tells me.

282
00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:46.680
Now, we have to come to this if we're going to have any real likeness to Jesus.

283
00:46:46.680 --> 00:46:52.680
So you yourself can say what other titles should be given to the cross.

284
00:46:52.680 --> 00:47:01.680
Then Louisa said, as you say, it can be said that the cross is festive, jubilant, joyful and desiring, in other words you should want it.

285
00:47:01.680 --> 00:47:15.680
And Jesus said, good, you spoke well. However, the soul comes to experience these effects of the cross when she is perfectly resigned to my will, only then.

286
00:47:15.680 --> 00:47:18.680
You don't get it theoretically.

287
00:47:18.680 --> 00:47:24.680
And also when she has given all of herself to me without keeping anything for herself.

288
00:47:24.680 --> 00:47:29.680
That's your Deuteronomy 6.4 to 10 again.

289
00:47:29.680 --> 00:47:34.680
And I so as not to be surpassed in love by the creature, give her all of myself.

290
00:47:34.680 --> 00:47:40.680
And in giving myself I also give the cross, which is my speciality.

291
00:47:40.680 --> 00:47:46.680
And the soul recognizing it as my gift makes feasts and rejoices.

292
00:47:46.680 --> 00:47:53.680
That does not mean that your festivity takes the pain away, it doesn't.

293
00:47:53.680 --> 00:47:59.680
So March the 20th, 1904.

294
00:47:59.680 --> 00:48:03.680
All things take their origin from faith.

295
00:48:03.680 --> 00:48:12.680
Now in Volume 2 we were told that faith is the eyes of the soul, gives your ability to see.

296
00:48:12.680 --> 00:48:19.680
This morning I was feeling all discouraged, Louisa said, and embittered because of the loss of my adorable Jesus.

297
00:48:19.680 --> 00:48:25.680
And while I was in this state, he let his most sweet voice be heard saying to me,

298
00:48:25.680 --> 00:48:30.680
"My daughter, all things take their origin from faith."

299
00:48:30.680 --> 00:48:34.680
One who is strong in faith is strong in suffering.

300
00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:38.680
Faith makes one find God in every place.

301
00:48:38.680 --> 00:48:45.680
It makes one see him in every action and touch him in every movement.

302
00:48:45.680 --> 00:48:51.680
And every new occasion that presents itself is a new divine revelation that one receives.

303
00:48:51.680 --> 00:48:55.680
Therefore remain strong in faith.

304
00:48:55.680 --> 00:49:00.680
But if you are strong in it, in all states and circumstances,

305
00:49:00.680 --> 00:49:08.680
faith will administer fortitude to you and will make you always united to God.

306
00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:18.680
Fortitude is the most wonderful gift of God, it's one of the great gifts, wisdom, understanding, counsel, fortitude,

307
00:49:18.680 --> 00:49:21.680
knowledge, piety, and the fear of the Lord.

308
00:49:21.680 --> 00:49:26.680
Now I always call fortitude steel for your soul.

309
00:49:26.680 --> 00:49:35.680
You know when they're building these high skyscrapers, they would not withstand high winds or hurricanes

310
00:49:35.680 --> 00:49:43.680
unless they had put steel girders into them to enable them to withstand the terrible storms.

311
00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:49.680
And the Lord knows that we are not able to withstand the storms of life

312
00:49:49.680 --> 00:49:54.680
if the steel girders of fortitude are not given to us.

313
00:49:54.680 --> 00:50:02.680
Now he says that faith opens you up to be able to receive fortitude, which is very important.

314
00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:09.680
So we go to April the 9th, 1904, and I have a VIP on this one as well.

315
00:50:09.680 --> 00:50:18.680
One act of perfect resignation is enough for the soul to be purged of any involuntary imperfection.

316
00:50:18.680 --> 00:50:22.680
Now this is extremely important.

317
00:50:22.680 --> 00:50:26.680
Now notice one act of perfect resignation.

318
00:50:26.680 --> 00:50:28.680
That means total resignation.

319
00:50:28.680 --> 00:50:36.680
Not a partial one, not a little bit, total, 100%, is enough to purge the soul of imperfections.

320
00:50:36.680 --> 00:50:39.680
It's incredible.

321
00:50:39.680 --> 00:50:46.680
This morning, Louisa said, since I would be receiving communion, I was thinking to myself,

322
00:50:46.680 --> 00:50:50.680
what will blessed Jesus say when he comes into my soul?

323
00:50:50.680 --> 00:50:54.680
He will say how ugly, bad, cold, abominable this soul is.

324
00:50:54.680 --> 00:50:57.680
Of course the Lord doesn't look at us like that.

325
00:50:57.680 --> 00:51:05.680
How quickly he will make the species be consumed so as not to be in contact with someone this ugly.

326
00:51:05.680 --> 00:51:13.680
Now it takes the species of the Eucharist 15 minutes to be consumed in us whether you're good or bad.

327
00:51:13.680 --> 00:51:15.680
That's the length of time it takes.

328
00:51:15.680 --> 00:51:22.680
And Louisa thinks that the species will be consumed faster because she is so-called ugly.

329
00:51:22.680 --> 00:51:31.680
Well what can I do? Even though I am so bad, yet you must have patience in coming because you are necessary to me anyway.

330
00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:34.680
Now here she's touching on something very important.

331
00:51:34.680 --> 00:51:38.680
That whether we're good or bad, we need Jesus desperately.

332
00:51:38.680 --> 00:51:42.680
We need God desperately. We need him for absolutely everything.

333
00:51:42.680 --> 00:51:49.680
And the weaker we are and the more sinful we are, the more we need him, not the less.

334
00:51:49.680 --> 00:51:54.680
So you are necessary to me anyway and I cannot be without you.

335
00:51:54.680 --> 00:52:02.680
Put there John 15-5 where Jesus said without me you can do nothing, meaning nothing good.

336
00:52:02.680 --> 00:52:08.680
At that moment Jesus came out from within my interior and he told me, my daughter,

337
00:52:08.680 --> 00:52:12.680
do not want to afflict yourself like this.

338
00:52:12.680 --> 00:52:19.680
In other words, don't put your will into this, don't start wallowing in this.

339
00:52:19.680 --> 00:52:22.680
It takes nothing to remedy it.

340
00:52:22.680 --> 00:52:32.680
Just one act of perfect resignation to my will is enough for you to be purged of all this ugliness that you talk about.

341
00:52:32.680 --> 00:52:36.680
And I will say to you the opposite of what you think.

342
00:52:36.680 --> 00:52:47.680
I will say to you how beautiful you are. I feel the fire of my love in you and the perfume of my fragrances, Proverbs 27-9.

343
00:52:47.680 --> 00:52:52.680
With you I want to make my perpetual dwelling and he disappeared.

344
00:52:52.680 --> 00:52:56.680
Now there's two things going on here.

345
00:52:56.680 --> 00:53:03.680
One is Louisa is giving a very negative rendering of who she is and what she's like.

346
00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:11.680
The Lord doesn't look at us like that and if we dwell on that we can shift very quickly into a self-pity party.

347
00:53:11.680 --> 00:53:19.680
Poor me, I'm weak and I'm miserable and I'm just that and the other and what can you expect and I'm a failure and so on and so forth.

348
00:53:19.680 --> 00:53:22.680
Cracked stuff, it's not necessary.

349
00:53:22.680 --> 00:53:28.680
The Lord doesn't look at us like that and he says that with all your misery and with all your weakness and everything,

350
00:53:28.680 --> 00:53:37.680
if you surrender totally to the divine will absolutely a magnificent act of surrender, it cleans all that stuff up.

351
00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:52.680
One second, it's a bit like a child coming in from playing outside and they've got scratches on their knees and the dresser, the trousers is dirty and in one movement the mother can actually heal it all.

352
00:53:52.680 --> 00:53:58.680
She just gives the child a kiss on the scratch and the kiss is miraculously works the thing.

353
00:53:58.680 --> 00:54:07.680
As far as the child is concerned, it is healed with that kiss and sometimes one movement of the hand will take the dart off the clothes as well.

354
00:54:07.680 --> 00:54:14.680
This is Jesus saying just one act of surrender will heal it and don't put your mind into that.

355
00:54:14.680 --> 00:54:21.680
Then when the confessor came, Louisa said, I told him everything and he said that it wasn't right.

356
00:54:21.680 --> 00:54:26.680
In other words, that you could be completely cleaned up with one act of resignation.

357
00:54:26.680 --> 00:54:31.680
He said that it is sorrow that purges the soul and that resignation is nothing to do with it.

358
00:54:31.680 --> 00:54:39.680
So after I received communion, I said, Lord, the priest told me that what you said was not right.

359
00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:46.680
It's now wonderful. We tell God that he isn't right. Explain yourself better and let me know the truth.

360
00:54:46.680 --> 00:54:54.680
And he very kindly added, my daughter, when it is about voluntary sin, then it takes sorrow.

361
00:54:54.680 --> 00:55:01.680
But when it is about imperfections and weaknesses and coldness and the like and the soul has added nothing of her own,

362
00:55:01.680 --> 00:55:11.680
then a perfect act of resignation is enough. And if needed, she's also purged of this whole state of looking at herself like this.

363
00:55:11.680 --> 00:55:16.680
So you can't be in the divine will if it is voluntary sin.

364
00:55:16.680 --> 00:55:29.680
So when Jesus said that he was not talking about voluntary sin, he was simply talking about the ordinary weaknesses and the flotsam and jetsam of everyday life.

365
00:55:29.680 --> 00:55:39.680
So, and if needed, she is purged of this state because in doing this act, the soul first encounters the divine will,

366
00:55:39.680 --> 00:55:49.680
which purges her human will and embellishes it with its qualities. And then she identifies herself with me.

367
00:55:49.680 --> 00:55:54.680
So you really need to think about that one. It's very freeing.

368
00:55:54.680 --> 00:56:06.680
So April the 10th, 1904, the three little ropes that bind Jesus all over and clasp him more intimately to the soul.

369
00:56:06.680 --> 00:56:14.680
This morning, finding myself with the fear that blessed Jesus in seeing me so bad had left me,

370
00:56:14.680 --> 00:56:27.680
I've felt him come out from within my interior and he told me, my daughter, why do you occupy yourself with useless thoughts and with things which are not?

371
00:56:27.680 --> 00:56:41.680
In other words, she's not bad. She's not sinning and all the rest of it. So just feeling a bit down is no reason for indulging in all of this stuff.

372
00:56:41.680 --> 00:56:57.680
I want to give you a whole lot of scriptures for this. Luke 11, 17, 1 Corinthians 13, 11, 2 Corinthians 10, 5, that is every thought must be captured and given to Christ.

373
00:56:57.680 --> 00:57:09.680
So you don't wallow in all of this stuff. And Isaiah 55, 8, the Lord's word has the power to do what it says.

374
00:57:09.680 --> 00:57:19.680
So if the Lord tells you to not worry about this stuff, you stop worrying about it because it's utterly useless to do that.

375
00:57:19.680 --> 00:57:32.680
So know that you have three titles before me which are like three little ropes and bind me all over and clasp me more intimately to you.

376
00:57:32.680 --> 00:57:45.680
In such a way that I cannot leave you and these three ropes are assiduous sufferings. That means you suffer courageously for years.

377
00:57:45.680 --> 00:57:53.680
Perpetual reparation for everybody else. So that means she's loving God all the time and persevering love.

378
00:57:53.680 --> 00:58:03.680
If you as a creature are constant in this, would the creator perhaps be inferior to the creature or would he himself let him be surpassed by her?

379
00:58:03.680 --> 00:58:10.680
And he says, absolutely not. So he said, this is what I see. You're not seeing things correctly.

380
00:58:10.680 --> 00:58:20.680
People often say that when they themselves look in a mirror, they don't see what other people see in them, which is actually true.

381
00:58:20.680 --> 00:58:29.680
April the 11th, 1904. Jesus thanks, Louisa. Imagine God thanking us.

382
00:58:29.680 --> 00:58:38.680
"Continue in my usual state," Louisa said, "after much struggling, I saw my adorable Jesus for just a little, and he told me,

383
00:58:38.680 --> 00:58:47.680
'You who wanted me so much, what do you want? What is it that you care about the most?'

384
00:58:47.680 --> 00:58:57.680
And Louisa said, 'Lord, I want nothing. What I care about the most is you alone.' So she's seeking him out of pure love.

385
00:58:57.680 --> 00:59:05.680
And he repeated, 'What you want, nothing?' All he gets are laundry lists from everybody else.

386
00:59:05.680 --> 00:59:18.680
'Ask me for something sanctity, grace, virtues, for I can give you everything.' And Louisa again said, 'Nothing. Nothing. I want you alone. And I want whatever you want.'

387
00:59:18.680 --> 00:59:24.680
And again he added, 'So you want nothing else? I alone am enough for you.'

388
00:59:24.680 --> 00:59:35.680
Remember, one of the most famous statements of Saint Teresa of Avila is that God alone suffices it. Well, very few people reach that level of loving God

389
00:59:35.680 --> 00:59:41.680
that they want only God and they don't want all the benefits that go with him.

390
00:59:41.680 --> 00:59:52.680
And so Jesus said, 'Your desires have no other life in you but for me alone. All your trust then must be for me alone.

391
00:59:52.680 --> 01:00:00.680
For even if you want nothing, you will obtain everything. God will still give you everything.'

392
01:00:00.680 --> 01:00:07.680
And without giving me any more time, he disappeared like a flash. Okay.

393
01:00:07.680 --> 01:00:26.680
In 2 Corinthians 6, and I think it's verses 1 to 11, but I could be wrong there, one of the things that Paul says is that he ends up a whole dissertation by saying, 'And as having nothing, we possess all things.' Okay.

394
01:00:26.680 --> 01:00:37.680
So, Louisa remained very disappointed, especially because as much as she asked for him, he would not come back.

395
01:00:37.680 --> 01:00:51.680
So she thought to herself, 'I want nothing. I think and care about nothing but him alone. While he seems not a bother about me, I don't know how his good heart can reach such a point.'

396
01:00:51.680 --> 01:01:01.680
She desires him so much and she loves him so much that she cannot reason about the privation.

397
01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:17.680
But those of us who have been studying this now for six volumes know that the reason for the privation is that he is out there dealing with the human race as he must do in order to keep it alive and to keep it growing.

398
01:01:17.680 --> 01:01:23.680
But Louisa thinks that he should be paying her all of this attention.

399
01:01:23.680 --> 01:01:39.680
And Louisa said, 'I spoke a lot of other nonsense. Now at that moment he came back and he said, 'Thank you. Thank you. What is greater when the creator tanks the creature or when the creature tanks the creator?'

400
01:01:39.680 --> 01:02:01.680
'Now know that when you wait for me and I delay in coming, I thank you. When I come immediately you are obliged to thank me. So does it seem trivial to you that the creator gives you an opportunity or the occasion to have him obliged to give thanks to his creature?'

401
01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:20.680
Now what Jesus is trying to do here is tell her, 'Please realise that everything, every single iota, for every single moment that's happening to you is all part of the will of God. It's not outside of the will of God. It's all part of it.'

402
01:02:20.680 --> 01:02:41.680
And that if you patiently wait for the Lord, that's Isaiah, I think it's 30/41, I think it is. Those who wait for the Lord shall renew their strength, they shall mount up with wings like the eagle.

403
01:02:41.680 --> 01:03:04.680
They shall run and not be weary. They shall walk and not faint.' So he's telling Louisa that she's been given the opportunity to wait for the Lord and to wait with hope and to wait with love and to wait with strength and all the rest of it.

404
01:03:04.680 --> 01:03:11.680
And then give him an opportunity to say thanks, because nobody else is doing it. Nobody else is showing him this kind of love.

405
01:03:11.680 --> 01:03:37.680
So April the 12th, 1904, peace is the greatest treasure. This morning, Louisa said, 'I felt disturbed because of the absence of blessed Jesus, and then after much struggling, I saw him for just a little.'

406
01:03:37.680 --> 01:03:51.680
And he told me, 'My daughter, when a river is exposed to the rays of the sun, in looking into it, one sees the same sun that is there in the heavens, obviously reflected in the water.'

407
01:03:51.680 --> 01:04:05.680
However, this happens when the river is calm, with no wind that ripples its waters. But if the waters are rippled, even though the river is completely exposed to the sun, you can see nothing.

408
01:04:05.680 --> 01:04:12.680
Everything's confusion because the water is tumbling all over the place. It is the same for the soul.

409
01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:23.680
When she is exposed to the rays of the divine sun, if she's calm, she perceives the divine sun within herself. She feels its heat.

410
01:04:23.680 --> 01:04:34.680
She sees the light and understands the truth. But if she's disturbed, even though she has it within herself, she feels nothing but confusion and disturbance.

411
01:04:34.680 --> 01:04:43.680
Therefore, hold peace as your greatest treasure, because God is a God of peace.

412
01:04:43.680 --> 01:04:57.680
And when we're at peace inside of our souls, then we are in a position where we can actually commune with him, we can recognise his presence, we can benefit from his presence, and all of that.

413
01:04:57.680 --> 01:05:08.680
So I want to give you the Philippians 4-7, the peace that passes all understanding and guards our hearts and our minds in Christ Jesus.

414
01:05:08.680 --> 01:05:17.680
I want to give you Romans 8-6 and 1 Corinthians 7-15.

415
01:05:17.680 --> 01:05:32.680
So, April 14, 1904. If the soul gives to God the food of patient love, God will give her the sweet bread of grace.

416
01:05:32.680 --> 01:05:42.680
Louisa said, "I continue in my usual state, but always with immense bitterness in my soul because of the privation of blessed Jesus.

417
01:05:42.680 --> 01:05:51.680
At the most he comes when I can take no more, and after I have almost persuaded myself that he will never come again.

418
01:05:51.680 --> 01:06:05.680
I saw him for just a little, carrying a chalice in his hand, and he told me, "My daughter, if in addition to the food of love, you give me the bread of your patients."

419
01:06:05.680 --> 01:06:10.680
That's the patience in waiting for him that Isaiah speaks about.

420
01:06:10.680 --> 01:06:26.680
If you give me the bread of your patients, because patience and suffering, patient and suffering love is a more solid, more nourishing and more fortifying food.

421
01:06:26.680 --> 01:06:32.680
Because if love is not patient, it can be said that it is empty.

422
01:06:32.680 --> 01:06:50.680
Now, beside that I want you to put 1 Corinthians 13-7, where St Paul says that love is patient and kind, but we forget to show some patience and kindness to the Lord, as well as to others.

423
01:06:50.680 --> 01:07:04.680
If love is not patient, it can be said that it is empty, light love with no substance, and therefore it can be said that the necessary materials in order to form the bread of patience are lacking.

424
01:07:04.680 --> 01:07:12.680
So, if you give me this patience, I will give you the sweet bread of grace.

425
01:07:12.680 --> 01:07:35.680
Now, notice the Lord is specifically asking for patience, and while saying this, he gave me to drink from what was inside the chalice that he carried in his hand, and it seemed sweet like a sort of liquor, which I am unable to distinguish, and then he disappeared.

426
01:07:35.680 --> 01:07:48.680
So, he gave her a soothing drink to fortify her to deal with this privation that she has to endure all her life.

427
01:07:48.680 --> 01:08:05.680
After this, Louisa said, "I saw many foreign people around my bed, priests, gentlemen, women, and it seemed that they were going to come and visit me."

428
01:08:05.680 --> 01:08:20.680
He has manifested to her and the graces he has given to her, because the Lord has manifested to us since 1882, okay, that he would choose a victim.

429
01:08:20.680 --> 01:08:33.680
Now, Louisa was born in 1865, so these people are obviously spiritual people, and the Lord has told them that a great victim would be given.

430
01:08:33.680 --> 01:08:47.680
So, she's about 17 at the time, that when they get this message, and the sign to recognize this victim would be that the Lord would keep her always in this state.

431
01:08:47.680 --> 01:08:59.680
In other words, that Louisa would have this extraordinary life, like a young woman, just as she was when he chose her without aging or changing in her very nature.

432
01:08:59.680 --> 01:09:10.680
Now, while they were saying this, I don't know, I saw myself just as I was when I became bedridden without having changed a bit after being in this state for several years.

433
01:09:10.680 --> 01:09:23.680
In other words, this is an instant which is illustrated when she was about 17 years of age, absolutely amazing what happens on a spiritual level.

434
01:09:23.680 --> 01:09:31.680
So, the next message is April the 16th, 1904.

435
01:09:31.680 --> 01:09:36.680
Jesus and God the Father speak about mercy to Louisa.

436
01:09:36.680 --> 01:09:49.680
"Continue in my usual state," Louisa said, "I found myself outside of myself, and I saw a multitude of people, and in their midst one could hear noises of bombs and gunshots.

437
01:09:49.680 --> 01:09:56.680
People were dropping dead or wounded, and those who are left would flee up to a palace nearby.

438
01:09:56.680 --> 01:10:02.680
But the enemies would go up there and kill them more surely than those who remained outside.

439
01:10:02.680 --> 01:10:13.680
So, I said to myself how I wish I could see whether the Lord is there in the midst of these people, so as to say to him, have mercy, have pity on these poor people.

440
01:10:13.680 --> 01:10:23.680
So, I went round and round and I saw Jesus as a little child, but little by little he kept growing until he reached the perfect age.

441
01:10:23.680 --> 01:10:30.680
I drew near him and I said, "Amyable Lord, don't you see the tragedy that is happening?

442
01:10:30.680 --> 01:10:33.680
You don't want to make use of your mercy anymore?

443
01:10:33.680 --> 01:10:42.680
Do you perhaps want to keep this attribute as useless, which has always glorified your incarnate divinity,

444
01:10:42.680 --> 01:10:55.680
with so much honor, forming a special crown on your august head, and be jeweling you with a second crown so wanted and loved by you, which is souls?"

445
01:10:55.680 --> 01:11:07.680
Now, while I was saying this, Jesus told me, "Enough, enough. Do not go any further. You want to speak of mercy, and what about justice?

446
01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:11.680
What are we going to do with it?"

447
01:11:11.680 --> 01:11:25.680
I told you that I repeat to you, it is necessary that justice follow its course, because the 20th century Jesus tells us in higher volumes was the most evil of all centuries.

448
01:11:25.680 --> 01:11:34.680
So, Louisa replied, "There's no remedy. Why then leave me on the earth when I can no longer placate you and suffer in the place of my neighbor?

449
01:11:34.680 --> 01:11:50.680
Since this is so, it's better if you let me die." At that moment, I saw another person behind the shoulders of blessed Jesus, and he told me, almost making a sign with his eyes, present yourself to my father and see what he tells you.

450
01:11:50.680 --> 01:12:19.680
I presented myself all trembling, and as soon as the father saw me, he told me, "Why have you come to me?" Now, this reminds me, sorry, of Elijah in 1 Kings 18, that after his wonderful triumph on Mount Carmel, dealing with the false prophets, he ran all the way to Mount Sinai, and God said to him, God the Father said to him, "What are you doing here? Why have you come?"

451
01:12:19.680 --> 01:12:32.680
And he asked him several times, so God the Father expects us all to deal with Jesus and to go through Jesus, because he's the mediator between God and man, so he says, "Why have you come?"

452
01:12:32.680 --> 01:12:47.680
And Louisa said, "Adorable goodness, infinite mercy, knowing that you are mercy itself. I have come to ask for your mercy on your very images, because all human beings were made in the image of God."

453
01:12:47.680 --> 01:13:13.680
That's Romans 829, and it's Genesis 1, 27. I want you to have mercy on your very images, mercy on the works created by you, mercy on nothing else but your creatures themselves, and he said to me, "So, it's mercy you want."

454
01:13:13.680 --> 01:13:27.680
But if you want true mercy, after justice had pours itself out, it will produce abundant fruits of mercy. Now, there's an incredible revelation.

455
01:13:27.680 --> 01:13:39.680
We think that mercy should be God letting us off the hook, but you know, if you let an offender off the hook too often, they only become worse,

456
01:13:39.680 --> 01:13:51.680
and they think that nobody will ever put any kind of discipline on them, but if you discipline them, then there is some chance that mercy can work afterwards.

457
01:13:51.680 --> 01:13:59.680
And this is what God the Father says, "After justice has poured itself out, it will produce abundant fruits of mercy."

458
01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:07.680
In other words, judgment is actually required, and that were the two world wars in the 20th century.

459
01:14:07.680 --> 01:14:26.680
Not knowing what else to say, I said, "Father, infinitely holy. When servants or people in need present themselves before their masters are rich people, if these are good, even if they do not give everything that is necessary for them, they give something."

460
01:14:26.680 --> 01:14:46.680
Now, here's Louisa being really bold and courageous in her intercessions. And you have to remember Abraham in Genesis 18, verses 22 to 32, when he was interceding with the Father for Sodom and Gomara.

461
01:14:46.680 --> 01:15:00.680
And he realized he wasn't going to get the whole thing. He said, "What about 50 good souls were there?" And then maybe it was only 40, maybe it was only 30, and he keeps on going down to maybe there's only five.

462
01:15:00.680 --> 01:15:13.680
In fact, there wasn't any, because a lot and his family were benefiting from all the terrible life that was going on there, so they weren't good, but they were saved because of Abraham.

463
01:15:13.680 --> 01:15:19.680
So here's Louisa being very courageous in her intercession.

464
01:15:19.680 --> 01:15:29.680
So she says, "These rich people and these kings always give something, and to me who have had the good of presenting myself before, the good means the privilege."

465
01:15:29.680 --> 01:15:35.680
You need to write the word "privilege therapy" or "I-V-I-L-E-G-E."

466
01:15:35.680 --> 01:15:50.680
You who have had the privilege of presenting myself before you absolute master of the universe, rich without limit infinite goodness, don't you want to give anything of what this poor little one has asked of you?

467
01:15:50.680 --> 01:16:00.680
Does a master perhaps not remain more honored and content when he gives than when he denies what is necessary to his servants?

468
01:16:00.680 --> 01:16:08.680
And after a moment of silence he added, "For love of you, instead of doing ten, I will do five."

469
01:16:08.680 --> 01:16:13.680
In other words, he gives her 50%. That's unbelievable.

470
01:16:13.680 --> 01:16:21.680
Just for one person interceding, powerfully before the throne of God, that the chastisement would be mitigated 50%.

471
01:16:21.680 --> 01:16:34.680
Our blessed lady has told us in Magigoria that wars could be stopped and chastisement mitigated if we did the fasting and the penance.

472
01:16:34.680 --> 01:16:46.680
Having said this, they disappeared and in several places of the earth, especially in Europe, I saw wars, civil wars and revolutions happen and multiply.

473
01:16:46.680 --> 01:17:05.680
At the time you need to realize that in France, the terrible scourge of rationalism began with the French Revolution, and France was the origin of the terrible tide of atheistic materialism that has swept the earth.

474
01:17:05.680 --> 01:17:17.680
And so there are consequences to that because, therefore, France is actually responsible for the terrible things that have happened afterwards.

475
01:17:17.680 --> 01:17:23.680
So let's take April the 21st, 1904.

476
01:17:23.680 --> 01:17:36.680
One who has the title of victim can fight with justice. In other words, Louisa, because of her victim soul status, she can take this approach with God.

477
01:17:36.680 --> 01:17:46.680
So continue in my usual state, Louisa said, "I felt people around my bed praying to our Lord, but I did not care about hearing what they wanted.

478
01:17:46.680 --> 01:17:53.680
I only cared about the fact that it was late and blessed Jesus had not made himself seen.

479
01:17:53.680 --> 01:17:57.680
Oh, my heart was tormented, fearing that he might not come at all.

480
01:17:57.680 --> 01:18:05.680
And I said to myself, "Blessed Lord, we are now at the last hour, and you're still not coming.

481
01:18:05.680 --> 01:18:10.680
Please do not give me this sorrow. Let yourself be seen at least."

482
01:18:10.680 --> 01:18:21.680
And while I was saying this, he came out from within my interior and said to those who are around me, "It is not licit for creatures to fight with my justice."

483
01:18:21.680 --> 01:18:32.680
Only for one who has the title of victim soul is it allowable or licit, not only to fight but to play with justice.

484
01:18:32.680 --> 01:18:43.680
And this, because in fighting or playing, one easily suffers, blows defeats and losses, and the victim is ready to receive the blows upon herself

485
01:18:43.680 --> 01:18:53.680
and to resign herself in the defeats and the losses without caring about her losses, about her sufferings, but only about the glory of God and the good of her neighbor.

486
01:18:53.680 --> 01:19:09.680
There's your Hebrews 12-2 again. Now, notice that Jesus is saying that those of us who are not victim souls, who are not prepared to take the punishment that other people deserve upon ourselves,

487
01:19:09.680 --> 01:19:22.680
and we're not prepared to take the blows of divine justice in order to save other people, that we do not have the right to actually make the kind of intercession that victim souls make.

488
01:19:22.680 --> 01:19:34.680
If I wanted to placate myself, Jesus said, "I have my victim here who was ready to fight and to receive all the fury of my justice upon herself."

489
01:19:34.680 --> 01:19:44.680
It shows that they were praying in order to placate the Lord, and I was left mortified and more embittered and hearing this from our Lord.

490
01:19:44.680 --> 01:19:53.680
Okay, so we'll do one more segment this evening. That's April the 26th, 1904.

491
01:19:53.680 --> 01:20:07.680
The habit doesn't make the monk. Now, this is a very important, I want to put a VIP on this, and you're going to hear a lot about the importance of placing the intention whenever we're praying.

492
01:20:07.680 --> 01:20:24.680
This morning, as I was outside of myself, I found myself with baby Jesus in my arms, surrounded by various devoted people and priests, many of whom were intent on vanities, luxury, and on fashions.

493
01:20:24.680 --> 01:20:33.680
And it seemed that they were saying that ancient proverb among themselves, "The habit doesn't make the monk."

494
01:20:33.680 --> 01:20:44.680
Blessed Jesus told me, "My beloved, oh, how defroded I feel of the glory which the creature owes me, and which I am denied with so much cheek.

495
01:20:44.680 --> 01:20:50.680
And even by persons who are said to be devout, that means they are religious."

496
01:20:50.680 --> 01:21:05.680
On hearing this, I said, "Dear little one of my heart, let us recite the three glory be's, placing the intention of giving to your divinity all the glory that the creature owes it."

497
01:21:05.680 --> 01:21:10.680
Now, notice the importance of placing the intention.

498
01:21:10.680 --> 01:21:21.680
"So you will receive at least reparation." And he said, "Yes, yes, let us recite them." So we recited them together.

499
01:21:21.680 --> 01:21:31.680
Then we recited one Hail Mary, placing the intention of giving the Queen Mother also all the glory that creatures owe her.

500
01:21:31.680 --> 01:21:44.680
"Oh, how beautiful it was to pray with blessed Jesus. I felt so much at ease and I said, 'My beloved, how I would like to make the profession of faith in your hands by reciting the creed together with you.'"

501
01:21:44.680 --> 01:21:49.680
Now, that's funny. How can Jesus make an act of faith in himself?

502
01:21:49.680 --> 01:22:02.680
So Jesus said, "At the creed you will have to recite by yourself, because that's for you, not for me, and you will say it in the name of all creatures so as to give me more glory and honor."

503
01:22:02.680 --> 01:22:11.680
Now, we have to remember every time we say the creed, we say it in reparation for all unbelief on behalf of all souls.

504
01:22:11.680 --> 01:22:26.680
So, Louisa said, "I placed my hands in his and I recited the creed. After this blessed Jesus told me, 'My daughter, it seems that I feel more relieved and that the black cloud of human ingratitude.'"

505
01:22:26.680 --> 01:22:36.680
Look at that. Throughout the 36 volumes, the human race is identified as completely ungrateful for all that God has done.

506
01:22:36.680 --> 01:22:43.680
And the black cloud of human ingratitude, especially from devout souls, has been moved away.

507
01:22:43.680 --> 01:22:58.680
Ah, my daughter, the external action has so much strength to penetrate into one's interior as to form a material garment for the soul.

508
01:22:58.680 --> 01:23:09.680
And when the divine touch touches them, they do not feel it vividly because their souls are wrapped in a muddy garment of earth understood.

509
01:23:09.680 --> 01:23:27.680
And since they do not feel the liveliness of grace, that muddy garment means all, they influence the television and the media and your gadgets and absolutely everything else, the newspapers and all the rest of it give to you, taking away your spiritual sight.

510
01:23:27.680 --> 01:23:34.680
And since they do not feel the liveliness of grace, grace is either rejected or remains fruitless.

511
01:23:34.680 --> 01:23:44.680
Oh, how difficult it is to enjoy pleasures, to dress luxuriously on the outside, and to despise those things internally.

512
01:23:44.680 --> 01:23:52.680
In other words, if you're going for fancy clothes and if you're going for fancy holidays and all the rest of it, that affects your soul.

513
01:23:52.680 --> 01:24:00.680
There's no way it doesn't affect your soul. Every single decision of ours does affect our souls.

514
01:24:00.680 --> 01:24:09.680
And so we can be actually responsible for our own spiritual blindness.

515
01:24:09.680 --> 01:24:23.680
So Jesus says how difficult it is to enjoy pleasures, to dress luxuriously on the outside, and to despise those things internally.

516
01:24:23.680 --> 01:24:36.680
On the contrary, the opposite occurs that that is one loves in his interior and enjoys what surrounds him externally. Oh dear, it penetrates into your innermost being.

517
01:24:36.680 --> 01:24:48.680
My daughter, consider yourself what the sorrow of my heart is in these times in seeing my grace being rejected by all kinds of people.

518
01:24:48.680 --> 01:24:56.680
While all my consolation is assisting creatures and the whole life of creatures is divine help.

519
01:24:56.680 --> 01:25:06.680
The sadness is that the whole of society and the whole Western world particularly have gone very far from this. It's really, really sad.

520
01:25:06.680 --> 01:25:15.680
But creatures reject my assistance and my help. You come to take part in my sorrow and sympathize with my bitterness.

521
01:25:15.680 --> 01:25:23.680
Having said this, he disappeared and I remained all afflicted because of the pains of my adorable Jesus.

522
01:25:23.680 --> 01:25:26.680
So I'm going to leave it there for this segment.
